course: dictionary
lesson: 9748
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Superior can mean better, higher in rank, or acting as if you are better than others. To pick the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Lake Superior, between Canada and the United States, is the largest freshwater lake by area.» Here superior is part of a name. Lake Superior is one of the Great Lakes, so it is not telling you the lake is better than the others. Capital letters at the start of a name are a clue.
explain: «one cake which was two feet across and three feet thick» is described by Kipling as «a Superior Comestible». The bracket tells you comestible means something to eat, so the cake is being called something special to eat. Read the clues, then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Superior means better in quality or more skilled than others, as in «superior goods».
fact: Superior also means higher in rank or position, as in «a superior officer».
fact: A superior smile is one that shows you think you are better than others, so it is not a friendly smile.
fact: A superior, in the noun form, is a person of higher rank, like a boss. Its plural is superiors.
fact: In maths, «superior to» is a formal way of saying «greater than» or «better than».
exercise: In an advert, «superior quality» means what? | Cheaper than others | *Better than others | Made in a hurry
exercise: In «Lake Superior», what kind of word is superior? | *Part of a name | A verb meaning to swim | An adjective meaning better
exercise: «The soldier had to obey his superiors.» Who are his superiors? | Other soldiers in his own rank | Animals in the field | *People of higher rank, like officers or bosses | Friends who live nearby
test: «He gave a superior smile, as if he knew more than everyone else.» What does superior suggest? | Feeling sorry for others | *Acting as if you are better than others | Being very tired
test: In maths, what does «superior to» mean? | *Greater than | Equal to | Less than | Next to
exam: Which sentence uses superior as a noun? | *The superior told the team to wait. | The superior smile annoyed her. | Superior goods cost more.
